Overlay patch 0020: byte-budget texture cache (reference 0020 ported;
Sync Wave 1 mandatory fix 5). Fast3D's texture cache is COUNT-based
(TEXTURE_CACHE_MAX_SIZE=1024) and the Metal DeleteTexture was EMPTY —
eviction never freed GPU memory, so big texture packs pin gigabytes and
jetsam at menu upload bursts after long sessions. Three parts: (1) virtual
GetTextureBytes (default 0 disables the budget on other backends);
(2) Metal DeleteTexture actually releases + exact allocatedSize ledger
(0019); (3) ImportTexture tail (__IOS__) evicts LRU entries to
gSohIos.TexCacheBudgetMB (default 1536, floor 128 entries).
FORK ADAPTATION: freed ids go to deferred_free_texture_ids (recycled next
frame) — this fork's own mid-frame-delete invariant (interpreter.cpp
TextureCacheDelete rationale); the Ship of Harkinian port recycled immediately. GPU
release itself is safe mid-frame (command buffers retain in-flight
textures).

